<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Law of Peace</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gayanashagowa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Law of Peace is the oral constitution of the Haudenosaunee, or Iroquois Confederacy. Tradition credits it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-peacemaker">the Peacemaker</a>, Deganawida, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiawatha">Hiawatha</a>, who persuaded the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca to end their feuds and join a league, usually dated to the 15th century. It set out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-council-qing">Grand Council</a> of chiefs and the role of clan mothers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-law-of-peace.jpg" alt="Great Law of Peace" width="320" height="164" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SargassoShearwater · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hiawatha_Belt_vector.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
